# Add project specific R8 rules here.
# AGP will combine all keep rule files in src/main/keepRules to pass to R8
#
# For more details, see
#   https://d.android.com/r/tools/r8/keep-rules

# Since AGP 9.1 R8 repackages classes into the unnamed package by default
# (equivalent to -repackageclasses), which is what makes the release DEX smaller.
# Together with the experimental `optimization.packageScope` configuration in
# app/build.gradle.kts this produced a broken DEX: R8 moved
# kotlin.sequences.SequencesKt___SequencesJvmKt (-> "qm1", unnamed package) out of
# its package, while its package-private superclass
# kotlin.sequences.SequencesKt__SequenceBuilderKt (-> "kotlin.sequences.d") stayed
# inside, so ART refused to load the class and the app crashed on startup with:
#   java.lang.IllegalAccessError: Class kotlin.sequences.d extended by class qm1
#   is inaccessible
# Opting out of repackaging keeps the package/access relationships of such
# synthetic Kotlin facade classes intact.
-dontrepackage

# If your project uses WebView with JS, uncomment the following
# and specify the fully qualified class name to the JavaScript interface
# class:
#-keepclassmembers class fqcn.of.javascript.interface.for.webview {
#   public *;
#}
